-- CODEX INSURANCE LIMITED -- hospitalization policy
-- L4 encoding of the coverage-determining logic.
-- This file carries no claim data: only the fact schema (copied verbatim
-- from inputs/schema.md), its two pre-defined helpers (also verbatim), and
-- the `covered` function plus whatever helpers `covered` needs.

IMPORT prelude

§ `Fact schema (verbatim from schema.md -- do not edit independently)`

DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF Sickness, `Accidental injury`, Neither

DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
  Skydiving, `Military service`, Firefighting, `Police service`, Other

DECLARE Claim
  HAS `agreement signed`                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `premium paid month`                         IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `hospitalization month`                      IS A NUMBER
      `hospitalization ground`                     IS A Ground
      `age at hospitalization`                     IS A NUMBER
      `causes`                                     IS A LIST OF Cause
      `fraud month`                                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `misrepresentation month`                    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit month`                       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit provider qualified`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `written confirmation month`                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `dispute arisen`                             IS A BOOLEAN
      `unable to settle month`                     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `arbitration commenced month`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `valid arbitration award issued`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `written proof of claim month`               IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `recovery sought month`                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `policy term months`                         IS A NUMBER

§§ `Supporting helpers (pre-defined -- call them, do not redefine them)`

GIVEN  `event month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
       `limit month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no later than` MEANS
  CONSIDER `event month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST m  THEN m AT MOST `limit month`

GIVEN  cs IS A LIST OF Cause
       c  IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arose out of` MEANS elem c cs

§ `1.1-1.3 Policy in effect`

-- 1.1 (opening clause): a benefit is only ever premised on a hospitalization
-- "for sickness or accidental injury". Ground's third constructor, Neither,
-- exists precisely to let a claim describe a hospitalization that is
-- neither of those (e.g. a deliberate, non-accidental act).
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`hospitalization is for sickness or injury` claim MEANS
  CONSIDER claim's `hospitalization ground`
    WHEN Sickness            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Accidental injury` THEN TRUE
    WHEN Neither              THEN FALSE

-- Generic existence check for a MAYBE-NUMBER "event month" field: TRUE
-- exactly when the event has happened at all, irrespective of which month.
-- Used for premium payment, fraud and misrepresentation -- none of which
-- carry a stated deadline in the contract, only a plain "has it occurred".
GIVEN `event month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`has happened` MEANS
  CONSIDER `event month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST anyMonth THEN TRUE

-- 1.1(2): "the applicable premium ... has been paid."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`premium paid` claim MEANS `has happened` (claim's `premium paid month`)

-- 1.3, second half: the wellness visit itself must have occurred no later
-- than the 6th month anniversary, with a qualified provider, AND written
-- confirmation of it supplied no later than the 7th month anniversary.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`wellness confirmation satisfied timely` claim MEANS
        `no later than` (claim's `written confirmation month`) 7
    AND `no later than` (claim's `wellness visit month`) 6
    AND claim's `wellness visit provider qualified`

-- 1.1(3): "The condition set out in Section 1.3 is still pending or has
-- been satisfied in a timely fashion." Evaluated as of the hospitalization
-- (the moment at which 1.1 asks whether the policy is "in effect"): before
-- the 7th month anniversary the condition has simply not yet come due
-- ("still pending"), so it cannot yet have been breached; from the 7th
-- month anniversary onward it must actually have been satisfied.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 1.3 condition met` claim MEANS
        claim's `hospitalization month` LESS THAN 7
    OR  `wellness confirmation satisfied timely` claim

-- 1.1(4)/1.2: "the policy has not been canceled." Cancelation happens on
-- fraud, on misrepresentation, or on expiry of the policy term (1.2); the
-- 1.3-non-satisfaction cancelation ground is already the "not still
-- pending, not yet satisfied" case of `section 1.3 condition met` above, so
-- it is not repeated here.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy in effect at hospitalization` claim MEANS
        claim's `agreement signed`
    AND `premium paid` claim
    AND `section 1.3 condition met` claim
    AND NOT `has happened` (claim's `fraud month`)
    AND NOT `has happened` (claim's `misrepresentation month`)
    AND claim's `hospitalization month` AT MOST claim's `policy term months`

§ `2.1 General exclusions`

-- Items 1-4: the hospitalization must not arise, directly or indirectly,
-- out of skydiving, military service, firefighting, or police service.
-- `causes` records what the sickness/injury arose out of, not the
-- claimant's occupation or status -- merely serving as a police officer,
-- for instance, does not by itself trigger the police-service exclusion.
-- Item 5: a standalone age threshold, not a "cause", so it is checked
-- against `age at hospitalization` directly rather than via `arose out of`.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`excluded under general exclusions` claim MEANS
        `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Skydiving
    OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Military service`
    OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Firefighting
    OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Police service`
    OR  claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

§ `3.2 Arbitration`

-- "such arbitration to be commenced within three (3) months from the day
-- such parties are unable to settle the dispute" -- a relative deadline
-- (3 months after `unable to settle month`), unlike the fixed anniversaries
-- in 1.3, so it is computed rather than passed as a literal `limit month`.
-- If the parties are not (yet) unable to settle, the clock has not started.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration timely commenced` claim MEANS
  CONSIDER claim's `unable to settle month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST u  THEN `no later than` (claim's `arbitration commenced month`) (u PLUS 3)

-- "Where there is a dispute or disagreement, the issuance of a valid
-- arbitration award shall also be a condition precedent to our liability."
-- Both this and timely commencement are conditioned on a dispute having
-- arisen at all; absent a dispute, arbitration is simply not in play.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`dispute specific conditions met` claim MEANS
  IF claim's `dispute arisen`
  THEN `arbitration timely commenced` claim AND claim's `valid arbitration award issued`
  ELSE TRUE

-- "In no case shall You seek to recover on this Policy before the
-- expiration of sixty (60) days after written proof of claim has been
-- submitted" -- this waiting period is NOT limited to disputed claims
-- ("in no case"), unlike the two conditions above. The schema is denominated
-- in months throughout, so 60 days is approximated here as 2 months.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`waiting period observed` claim MEANS
  CONSIDER claim's `written proof of claim month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST p THEN
      CONSIDER claim's `recovery sought month`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST r THEN r AT LEAST (p PLUS 2)

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration compliant` claim MEANS
        `dispute specific conditions met` claim
    AND `waiting period observed` claim

§ `covered`

-- Every field of Claim is used above except `causes` (used in the
-- exclusions check) and `hospitalization month` (used both in the 1.3
-- timing test and the policy-term test) -- both of which are used more than
-- once; every other field is used exactly once.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
covered claim MEANS
        `hospitalization is for sickness or injury` claim
    AND `policy in effect at hospitalization` claim
    AND NOT `excluded under general exclusions` claim
    AND `arbitration compliant` claim
